---
// Override for Starlight's default PageSidebar component. Stock Starlight
// renders TWO entirely separate right-column TOC UIs and swaps between
// them with CSS: a "mobile" dropdown pill (MobileTableOfContents, stock,
// never touched) below the lg breakpoint (1152px / 72rem), and our
// CollapsibleToc icon rail (wired in as the TableOfContents override, see
// astro.config.mjs) at/above it — both always rendered into the DOM,
// visibility toggled via the `lg:sl-hidden` / `lg:sl-block` utility
// classes. That's why ticket 23's icon-rail fixes never showed up for the
// maintainer: this app's default preview width sits under 1152px, so what
// they kept seeing was the completely separate, unmodified stock mobile
// pill the whole time — not our rail, not touched by any of that work.
//
// Renders just the rail, unconditionally, at every width instead — one
// floating-button design, not two components silently swapping under you.
// See .scratch/ew-wiki-real-build/issues/23-header-toc-layout-rework.md's
// Round 2.
import TableOfContents from 'virtual:starlight/components/TableOfContents';
---

{Astro.locals.starlightRoute.toc && <TableOfContents />}
